cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "bvar-toolkit: MATLAB code for large Bayesian VARs"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the paper whose method you use
  (see CITING.md) and this software record.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chan
    given-names: Joshua C. C.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3632-128X"
    affiliation: Purdue University
repository-code: "https://github.com/joshuaccchan/bvar-toolkit"
url: "https://joshuachan.org/code.html"
abstract: >-
  MATLAB code for estimating large Bayesian vector autoregressions. The
  repository archives fourteen replication packages verbatim and consolidates
  their shared machinery into a single tested library: samplers for stochastic
  volatility and VAR coefficients, shrinkage and asymmetric conjugate priors,
  forecasting routines, and marginal-likelihood estimators. Most library
  functions began as extractions from the packages, and unit tests check that
  they still reproduce the original code draw for draw under a fixed seed, at
  their default settings. Short examples show how to use each piece, and six
  tutorials answer questions from applied work with the settings of a
  published paper, with scripts that run the same analysis on other data.
keywords:
  - Bayesian econometrics
  - vector autoregression
  - stochastic volatility
  - Markov chain Monte Carlo
  - marginal likelihood
  - shrinkage priors
  - macroeconomic forecasting
  - MATLAB
license: MIT
